# Keep local state, secrets and caches out of the image and the build context.
# data/ matters most: COPY . . would otherwise bake a local sovereign.db into
# the image, and Docker seeds a new named volume from it. (To carry a local
# database into Docker on purpose, see "docker compose cp" in the README.)
# .env holds the API keys: compose hands it to the containers at start-up
# (env_file), so it never needs to be — and must never be — in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
.git
data/
logs/
backups/
contracts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
